_premise_retrieval","formal_math_readiness_gate","formal_math_verifier_trace_repair_loop","lean_std_premise_index","materials_chemistry_closed_loop_lab_safety_replay","mathematical_strategy_atlas_hypothesis_scorer","navigation_hologram_route_plane","pattern_assimilation_step","pattern_binding_contract","prediction_oracle_reconciliation","proof_diagnostic_evidence_spine","provider_context_recipe_budget_policy","public_reveal_walkthrough","research_replication_rubric_artifact_replay","ring2_premise_retrieval_precision_recall_harness","routing_anti_patterns_registry","spatial_world_model_counterfactual_simulation_replay","tactic_portfolio_availability_probe","target_shape_tactic_routing_gate","tool_server_pressure_inventory","undeclared_library_prior_symbol_classifier","verifier_lab_execution_spine","verifier_lab_kernel","world_model_projection_drift_control_room"],"exposed_count":0,"exposure":[],"failure_modes":[],"id":"P-6","kind":"principle","plain":"A missing piece of evidence, policy file, source digest, secret scan, negative case or self-scan of a result record blocks the result or lowers its status. A generated summary further downstream can explain why something passed, and it can never turn a blocked source into a pass.","principles":[],"reader":{"analogy":{"boundary":"The building picture covers why an uninspected part holds the whole back; a complete set of sign-offs still does not mean nothing was missed.","maps":[{"analogy":"the building is fit only if every trade passes, and the worst result decides","doctrine":"a combined status takes the lowest status of its parts"},{"analogy":"a trade with no inspection on file counts as failed","doctrine":"a part with no evidence counts as blocked"},{"analogy":"a later walk-through can downgrade the building and needs a fresh passing inspection to approve it","doctrine":"a later step may lower a status and needs new evidence to raise it"}],"text":"A building cannot be signed off for use until wiring, plumbing and fire safety have all passed. If the fire inspection never happened, the building stays unfit, and a later walk-through can find a new fault but cannot approve it alone."},"basis":"authored_reader_enrichment","counterexample":"A status board shows a component as green because no scan reported a problem, counting a check that never ran as a pass.","does_not_prove":"Failing closed decides what happens when evidence is missing; whether the parts that have evidence are correct is a separate question.","enforced_in_component_ids":["formal_math_readiness_gate","batch10_cold_eval_honesty_capsule","corpus_readiness_mathlib_absence_gate"],"example":{"component_ids":["formal_math_readiness_gate"],"text":"The formal-math readiness gate takes the lowest status among its inputs, so when the corpus or a required check is missing it reports blocked, and a later summary cannot change that to passing."},"governs":"How a combined status is built from its parts when some evidence is missing.","plain":"A combined result is only as sound as its weakest part. If one part has no evidence behind it, the whole counts as not ready. A later step can downgrade that verdict, and raising it takes fresh work.","potential_misread":"That an unchecked part is harmless and can count as a pass, or that a summary page can promote something that was blocked underneath it.","refuses":"A silent default pass, where missing evidence, a skipped scan or a summary page turns a blocked part green.","requires":"Taking the lowest status among the parts, treating any part with no evidence as blocked, and requiring new evidence before a later step raises a status.","source_ref":"core/doctrine_enrichment.json","why_it_matters":"A missing check or skipped scan cannot quietly count as approval."},"rests_on":["AX-5"],"source_ref":"PRINCIPLES.md::P-6","statement":"Grounding: AX-5.\nObligation grounding: AX-5.O1.composite_status_meets_parts, AX-5.O2.no_evidence_defaults_blocked, AX-5.O3.authority_cannot_raise_without_derivation.\n\nA missing piece of evidence, policy file, source digest, secret scan, negative\ncase or self-scan of a result record blocks the result or lowers its status. A\ngenerated summary further downstream can explain why something passed, and it\ncan never turn a blocked source into a pass.","statement_sha256":"01e3ac48fa91d043c7af4759fec7552be250d21ba894f4f7d52154a81ce7e660","title":"Status fails closed","violates":[]},"schema_version":"plectis_component_http_v1","snapshot_revision":"45be1deb333ad57cd9ae093229455d0a52d3bf23a9064cde09f1a6e16f4c7044"}